  "gameSpawnNote": "The direct route resolves a blueprint class that is ALREADY IN MEMORY, and Unreal loads one the first time the game creates it - so a class this server has never made cannot be placed directly. This table is the game's own admin command for the ones that have one, and what it says was DRIVEN on 2026-09-19 against game build 1.3.3.4 rather than read off the paks alone. `named` verbs take the spawn name, a count and the place: `SpawnAnimal BP_Deer 1 Location \"X=... Y=... Z=...\"` put a deer 83 cm from the point it was asked for. Their success is SILENCE and any sentence back from the game is a refusal. `atPlayer` is the BOSS answer and it is a capability rather than a refusal: both boss verbs really do spawn, and both put the boss on the player who ran the command. Four spellings were driven for the Razor and none aimed it - `Location \"X=...\"` and a bare quoted triplet each landed it on the player 120 m from the point asked for, and a quoted vector with no keyword created nothing that lasted; the Brenner landed on the player both bare and with a Location. That matches the game's own asset, where SpawnBrenner declares no argument at all and SpawnRazor declares one it evidently ignores. `spawnable: false` is a name the game itself refuses - the five abstract bases a puppet family is built on, which the direct route also faults on, leaving a pawn behind each time. A name in none of these has no admin command anywhere in the game's 233 and arrives only when an encounter, a bunker or a guarded post makes one.",
